# WebSocket via websocat. Opens an interactive terminal split:
# type a line + Enter to send, Ctrl-C (in terminal mode) to hang up.
# Body lines are sent as the first messages right after connecting.
#
# Local echo server (websocat can be one):
#   websocat -t ws-l:127.0.0.1:9000 mirror:

@ws = ws://localhost:9000

### connect and send two messages
WS {{ws}}

honk
honk honk

### auth via header on the handshake
WS {{ws}}/chat
Authorization: Bearer static-token

hello with a token

### auth via query string (common for browsers-first APIs)
WS {{ws}}/chat?token={{GOOSE_TOKEN}}

### Basic auth on the handshake
# @args --basic-auth gooseman:secret
WS {{ws}}/chat

### subprotocol + origin (some servers check these)
# @args --protocol graphql-ws --origin http://localhost
WS {{ws}}/graphql

{"type": "connection_init"}

### public TLS echo server
WS wss://echo.websocket.org

hello from gooseman
